    "description": "Vintage Calligraphy & Writing Collectible Set\nMixed Media Desk Set with Display Box\nWood, Glass, Metal, and Paper, 11 x 8 x 3 Inches\nThis comprehensive vintage writing and philatelic collection is housed in a decorative black wooden chest with a patterned interior lid. The set features classical tools for traditional correspondence, including both hand-blown glass and carved wooden dip pens, alongside an ornamental magnifying glass and a curated selection of mid-20th-century American postage stamps. Such sets were characteristic elements of personal stationery desks, appealing to calligraphy practitioners and historical ephemera collectors.\nHand-blown twisted glass dip pen and turned wooden pen handle with internal metal nib holder\n11 assorted metal pen nibs in various sizes for calligraphy and fine writing\nVintage-style magnifying glass featuring an ornate, relief-patterned metal handle\n6 vintage US postage stamps including 1949 Puerto Rico Inauguration (3c) and Noah Webster (4c) issues\nHinged black wooden box with dedicated storage compartments and a decorative patterned underside lid\nCondition:\nThe wooden box shows light exterior shelf wear and surface dust accumulation. The glass pen is intact with no visible chips to the spiral writing tip; includes a small protective sleeve. The wooden pen handle shows significant surface patina, staining, and finish wear consistent with age. Metal nibs show varying degrees of surface oxidation. Stamps are in used/mixed condition; one Noah Webster stamp has a visible tear and several show adhesive residue or hinging marks. Magnifying glass lens is clear with minor tarnishing to the metal frame.",
